# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for WasmEdge.
#
# Usage:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$PWD/utils/sanitizer/tsan.supp" ./wasmedgeLLVMCoreTests
#
# Only races that ThreadSanitizer cannot see the synchronization for belong
# here. A race in WasmEdge code is a bug to fix, not an entry to add.

# libgcc's registry of dynamically registered DWARF unwind tables.
#
# LLVM's JIT registers an EH frame for every module it materializes
# (__register_frame), and drops it again when the JIT instance dies. libgcc
# keeps those registrations in the lock-free B-tree of unwind-dw2-btree.h and
# rebalances it in place, so a node split memmoves entries that another thread
# is reading through _Unwind_Find_FDE. The B-tree is safe under exactly that
# access pattern -- it coordinates with version counters read and written
# through __atomic builtins -- but libgcc_s.so.1 ships uninstrumented, so
# ThreadSanitizer never observes those atomics and sees only the bare memmove.
#
# This suppresses any race whose stack reaches libgcc_s. In practice the only
# libgcc code a WasmEdge thread enters is the unwinder, so the reach is narrow;
# it does mean a race inside the unwinder itself would go unreported.
race:libgcc_s.so.1
